of the parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola.\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(-5,0)$ and $(2,0).$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=-5$ and $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "867af724-0aa0-599a-8a5f-ee753fd19414" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Parabola Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7677ae-e62e-5829-91f7-2020875a297a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ba/ba70051173652d8783cc8ebd9f200b5dcdf37cda8d81a772c0160e01c31cbf32.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561615} {:answer/id #uuid "21653903-a8ae-5843-86a3-6e201dd68978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/00/007a6abdf7787cc14e40c3d92996d5224904a656f8fa6ef42a9911ce97bc24a6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561674} {:answer/id #uuid "496c5471-4221-5e19-a1ab-408227761210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c3/c34cebb49b0482f02872a1ba68f73f8e931d8fb6583daf653560fc17f5b4831d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561770} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ac50e9-41c5-5f35-8129-bb0c31f3b0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/ae303cc7bd52ab5c6c5eb19f0ed3abe6286f560d58b6c21c78bac4758e978774.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561981} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3011dc-818d-5565-8b19-02f93ab49957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cfd42d5e800218639a82bbe46a0749bc3788c616fedc43cb704ebea9448a5867.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21653903-a8ae-5843-86a3-6e201dd68978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/00/007a6abdf7787cc14e40c3d92996d5224904a656f8fa6ef42a9911ce97bc24a6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561674} :answer-field/id #uuid "758cf8be-30e9-58cb-b2f3-197f61860574" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7984db9b-dab8-5221-ba35-8d0a5e549cba" :question/math-academy-id "q-106059" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the graph of $y={x}^{2}-x-6?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y={x}^{2}-x-6.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=-2,-1,0,1,2,3$ and then use the formula $y={x}^{2}-x-6$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row. \n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $0$ | $-4$ | $-6$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $0$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/4f/4fbf87172434c03bbdff6967d03eae3146f016dcdbb9422e89d2d94ab7693cd5.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/00/007a6abdf7787cc14e40c3d92996d5224904a656f8fa6ef42a9911ce97bc24a6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "867af724-0aa0-599a-8a5f-ee753fd19414" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Graph of a Parabola Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42e07ce2-bc8b-58a5-9504-4e7eb9582a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6ab5e5cdef936707ab8e9bd7fdc54c790ff4ce93cd3ef8af44aae44e8cd77764.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561744} {:answer/id #uuid "63e31f21-22da-5f21-b0c2-d0c9a0ddaefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f671cee2e37f7905c220357782d2d4f2e6361d4858030084492e216d3f3031cd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561824} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e97a60-753f-5d6a-af1d-3fcdedc3559c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/0779906575c293797e031d96b507cdcbd5f6380dcd497ea2885c059da07d6da7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561996} {:answer/id #uuid "a94ecbb5-eea4-59d0-b204-e4dcc12c3179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8fcd77fa59730639e108526ab31c73086db42e744353ff57a64f4df96c39a116.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562004} {:answer/id #uuid "b71126cb-562d-5bc2-bef7-a0e8477bbcdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b868ef7ef919776ed69ceea87aefaa46787794353e5b390c27368fe5dd66b972.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63e31f21-22da-5f21-b0c2-d0c9a0ddaefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f671cee2e37f7905c220357782d2d4f2e6361d4858030084492e216d3f3031cd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561824} :answer-field/id #uuid "636c8023-db68-55b4-ae54-78725778fd9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5c3534c-ace7-5657-a9dc-80aa55f51084" :question/math-academy-id "q-23981" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the graph of $y={x}^{2}-3x+5?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct a table of values for the function $y={x}^{2}-3x+5.$ We fill the first row with the $x$-values $x=-1,0,1,2,3,4$ and then use the formula $y={x}^{2}-3x+5$ to compute the corresponding $y$-values in the second row.\n\n| $\\,\\,x\\,\\,$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,\\,y\\,\\,$ | $9$ | $5$ | $3$ | $3$ | $5$ | $9$ |\n\nIf we plot those points on a graph, we can start to see the shape of a parabola:\n\n![](images/5a/5a7374c0e81f36d4d320abf38dcf72ac0b377c335894c601bfae82b64ea0bca3.png)\n\nWe fill out the graph by drawing the parabola through the plotted points:\n\n![](images/f6/f671cee2e37f7905c220357782d2d4f2e6361d4858030084492e216d3f3031cd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6aa081d4-f85a-5239-b034-b78894429611" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Roots of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cdb967f-21c2-5170-b53d-16d5028e4ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561620} {:answer/id #uuid "104e04eb-0268-563b-88fc-22075c061db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No roots" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561631} {:answer/id #uuid "756eb032-8a5b-5360-9dc8-c4731f589bca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-1$ and $x=8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561872} {:answer/id #uuid "96957528-289f-58b7-a316-2d142247431e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561955} {:answer/id #uuid "a197812f-198c-576c-b3c5-5d39d4ceb48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1$ and $x=-8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "104e04eb-0268-563b-88fc-22075c061db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No roots" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561631} :answer-field/id #uuid "88ac794d-2b1b-52d1-873f-37b7753f77b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d69fa39-1eb4-5e90-8609-317c0513eaff" :question/math-academy-id "q-24637" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4e5c26cd78c9f3e778f5396b2cfda357042ddacc467783cb657ed9d5364665c4.png)\n\nFind the roots of the parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The roots of a parabola are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola.\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the curve does not intercept the $x$-axis.\n\nTherefore, the parabola does not have any roots."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae1738d1-3261-5769-ab80-0edcc76ab6f3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Y-Intercept of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43df9d15-0eff-56bd-ae68-6ce404601e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561747} {:answer/id #uuid "9d110e39-d8dd-5043-9919-f6ab4ffa4686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561969} {:answer/id #uuid "ac8df273-fbbd-50d2-a745-504e98301f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562012} {:answer/id #uuid "b0efac7a-0fd5-5b62-92bc-2e8956c2a791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562021} {:answer/id #uuid "fc271961-d308-50c2-8c91-fd71f82862ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d110e39-d8dd-5043-9919-f6ab4ffa4686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561969} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce7f934-30bb-5661-a72f-65673ac7cfc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dcd95f6f-d031-5291-b596-6c28f4bcefd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-83559" :question/problem "![](images/ec/ecd951a63d500d0bf6b5234a65b8df55ada27882be337df6aea7d7aaa516e91b.png)\n\nThe equation of the curve above is $y=-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}x+k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if we substitute $x=0$ into the given equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}x+k \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{4}(0)^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}(0)+k \\\\ y & =k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nmeaning that the curve intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,k).$ Based on the graph, we can find that $k=\\frac{1}{2}$ since our parabola intercepts the $y$-axis at \n$(0,\\frac{1}{2}).$"}]}
